                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Connecting spend to value",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "13pt",
                      "color": "#4B2D83"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "For each credit tier, compare its share of spend (Credit Share %) with its share of value (Value Share %). When a tier's spend share sits well above its value share, its credits are outpacing the value it returns - review those users. The matrix pinpoints them: users in a high credit band but a low value band are the adjust list, while high value / low credit users are efficient stars to protect. Value per Credit is the quick justification test. Estimated Value $ is modeled from observed task counts using published time-per-task benchmarks and the selected customer labor rate. Credit Share %, credit tiers, and Value per Credit remain unavailable until observed consumption data and required customer billing inputs are connected. Value per Task divides the same modeled value by observed Cowork Tasks (Threads).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "8pt",
                      "color": "#1B1F27"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
